e,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":0.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.035364132745063406,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":58.5,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.10269406479038826,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":84.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.010115325199527597,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":87.4,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":-9.57301538085098e-05,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.12967591707443435,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":78.4,"_gate_incr_roic":0.057646821816130636,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":35.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.017511992117024366,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":39.2,"_gate_pool_share":-0.04664452536065422,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":21.3,"_gate_rev_durability":0.0515892871079906,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":50.8,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.027514758983702103,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":77.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0.05918834176884609,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":59.2,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.01000788402907658,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":22.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.008452176166251713,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":39.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004918317160028979,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.00153,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"WEC Energy Group, Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides regulated natural gas and electricity, and renewable and nonregulated renewable energy services in the United States. The company operates through Wisconsin, Illinois, Other States, Electric Transmission, and Non-Utility Energy Infrastructure segments. It generates and distributes electricity from coal, natural gas, oil, and nuclear, as well as renewable energy resources, including wind, solar, hydroelectric, and biomass; and distributes and hydroelectric natural gas. The company also owns, maintains, monitors, and operates electric transmission systems; and generates, distributes, and sells steam. As of December 31, 2025, the company operated approximately 35,200 miles of overhead distribution lines and 37,600 miles of underground distribution cables, as well as 420 electric distribution substations and 649,500 line transformers; approximately 47,200 miles of natural gas distribution mains; 1,300 miles of natural gas transmission mains; 2.4 million natural gas lateral services; 510 natural gas distribution and transmission gate stations; and 67.0 billion cubic feet of working gas capacities in underground natural gas storage fields. The company was formerly known as Wisconsin Energy Corporation and changed its name to WEC Energy Group, Inc. in June 2015. WEC Energy Group, Inc. was founded in 1896 and is headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott J. Lauber C.P.A. | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 59 | Compensation: $5.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the top quartile among Utilities peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["WEC Energy Group, Inc. is a large-cap utilities business with a $38.7B market cap on $9.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $1.0B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 36% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.36133381495638595},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"WEC Energy Group (NYSE:WEC) Stock: Insider Margaret Kelsey Sells 18,380 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/wec-energy-group-nysewec-stock-insider-margaret-kelsey-sells-18380-shares.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794492544.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.902,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Margaret C. Kelsey Executes 18,380 WEC Stock Options and Sells Shares on November 10, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/margaret-c-kelsey-executes-18380-wec-stock-options-and-sells-shares-on-november-10-2026","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794492331.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is WEC Energy (NYSE:WEC) Lifting Guidance on Data Centers?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/utility/is-wec-energy-nysewec-lifting-guidance-on-data-centers","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794406080.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"7,608 WEC Energy Group, Inc. $WEC Shares Sold by Commonwealth Equity Services LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/7608-wec-energy-group-inc-wec-shares-sold-by-commonwealth-equity-services-llc.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794386639.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.935,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"WEC Energy Group, Inc. (NYSE:WEC) Stock Has Average Price Target of $117.88 According to Analysts","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/wec-energy-group-inc-nysewec-stock-has-average-price-target-of-117-88-according-to-analysts.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794383306.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.827,"tier":0,"scope":"company